---
/**
 * The About page. It was the Maker page until 30 August 2026.
 *
 * The client's Part 6 answer changed the page's direction: no personal
 * profile, no name, no portrait, no career history at this stage. Structure &
 * Style is presented as a company, in "we", and this page explains what the
 * company does, the standard it works to, and what a client can expect. The
 * personal story may return later as the business develops; nothing here
 * forecloses that.
 *
 * Two constraints survive from the maker version:
 *
 * Section 10 of the tone protocol is still an absolute factual limit: no crew
 * nouns, no workshop, no manufacturing claimed as ours. Company voice does not
 * license a single plural that implies staff. The protocol's mandate to state
 * the one-person fact plainly on this page was struck on 30 Aug 2026 (defect
 * register item 21, closed: the client's Q60 company framing is the settled
 * permanent direction, accepted by Denis on the scaling logic). What this page
 * says is the accountability fact that survives both rules and any future
 * hire: the person who measures is the person who draws and fits.
 *
 * No portrait appears. Q56 was withdrawn with the rest of Part 6.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Wrap from "../components/ds/Wrap.astro";
import Display from "../components/ds/Display.astro";
import Kicker from "../components/ds/Kicker.astro";
import SectionHead from "../components/ds/SectionHead.astro";
import EnquireBand from "../components/ds/EnquireBand.astro";
import MonoLabel from "../components/ds/MonoLabel.astro";
import Link from "../components/ds/Link.astro";
import Value from "../components/Value.astro";

import { BUSINESS } from "../data/site";
import { BAND, CONTACT } from "../data/site-content";
import { indexable } from "../data/page-gates";

const isIndexable = indexable("/about/");

/**
 * The conduct practices, in the plain-word forms approved at tone protocol
 * v1.4 section 11. These are the only publishable conduct facts; nothing may
 * be added here without confirmation. The accountability fact (the person who
 * measured does the fitting) has its own section above and is not repeated.
 */
const CONDUCT = [
  "Floors covered in taped-down protective board, furniture wrapped and moved aside, doorways sealed with zipped dust screens.",
  "Dust extraction connected to every cutting tool, with an air scrubber running in the room.",
  "Cutting outside where access allows, otherwise in one sealed room. Never in a hallway or a communal area.",
  "8am to 5pm on weekdays in houses. In a managed block, whatever hours the building sets.",
  "Insurance and the safety paperwork go to the managing agent before the start date, with the building's sign-off in place before anything begins.",
  "The lift booked and protected before any delivery, with stair protection down on delivery days.",
  "The room vacuumed and the tools stacked at the end of every day, usable overnight.",
];
---

<Base
  title="About Structure & Style"
  description="What Structure & Style does, the standard the work is held to, and what to expect from a commission, from the first visit through to aftercare."
  noindex={!isIndexable}
>
  <Wrap style="padding-top:var(--hero-y);padding-bottom:var(--section-y)">
    <Kicker scribe>About</Kicker>
    <Display level={1} as="h1" style="margin:var(--space-12) 0 var(--space-13)">
      The standard we work to
    </Display>
    <p style="max-width:var(--measure);font-size:var(--type-lede);color:var(--text-quiet)">
      We design, measure, fit and finish bespoke furniture for London homes, and we run the whole
      commission from the first visit through to aftercare.
    </p>
  </Wrap>

  <Wrap style="padding-bottom:var(--section-y)">
    <SectionHead meta="Our approach" level={4}>How a commission runs</SectionHead>
    <p style="max-width:var(--measure)"><Value q="q06" /></p>
    <p style="max-width:var(--measure);margin-top:var(--space-8);color:var(--text-quiet)">
      Four stages, the same four every time: visit, survey and drawings, production, fitting.
      <Link href="/process/" variant="nav" style="margin-left:var(--space-5)">The full process, stage by stage</Link>
    </p>

    <div style="margin-top:var(--space-16)">
      <SectionHead meta="In plain terms" level={4}>The standard</SectionHead>
      <p style="max-width:var(--measure)"><Value q="q29" /></p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:var(--space-16)">
      <SectionHead meta="Accountability" level={4}>Who does the work</SectionHead>
      {/* The trades-coordination sentence that used to follow here was cut by
          the Truth gate 31 Aug 2026: it traced only to q06's PROVISIONAL note,
          never to a confirmed answer. It returns if Kaspar confirms it. */}
      <p style="max-width:var(--measure)">
        The person who measures your room is the person who draws it and the person who fits it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:var(--space-16)">
      <SectionHead meta="Design" level={4}>Before anything is ordered</SectionHead>
      <p style="max-width:var(--measure)">
        Every project gets a measured survey and a fixed, itemised quotation. Where design
        development is needed, a design week follows the quotation being accepted and the deposit
        paid: scaled drawings and elevations, issued for review. Up to two rounds of revisions are
        included, and any design cost sits inside the quotation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:var(--space-16)">
      <SectionHead meta="Materials" level={4}>Engineered board, on purpose</SectionHead>
      <p style="max-width:var(--measure)">
        Engineered board over solid timber is a considered choice rather than a compromise: more
        stable and more consistent. Real wood veneer carries the timber look where one is wanted.
        It also keeps large amounts of solid hardwood out of furniture that does not need them.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top:var(--space-8)">
        <Link href="/materials/" variant="nav" chamfer>The range, the finishes and the reasoning</Link>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:var(--space-16)">
      <SectionHead meta="In your home" level={4}>What to expect while we work</SectionHead>
      <p style="max-width:var(--measure)">
        The work happens inside a home that stays lived in. These are the working practices on
        every job.
      </p>
      <ul style="list-style:none;margin:var(--space-10) 0 0;padding:0;max-width:var(--measure);display:grid;gap:var(--space-7)">
        {CONDUCT.map((line) => (
          <li style="border-top:var(--rule-hair);padding-top:var(--space-6)">{line}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:var(--space-16)">
      <SectionHead meta="Afterwards" level={4}>Once the work is finished</SectionHead>
      <p style="max-width:var(--measure)"><Value q="q35" suffix="." /></p>
      <p style="max-width:var(--measure);margin-top:var(--space-8)">
        If doors or other moving parts settle within the 2-year aftercare period, we come back and
        adjust them. Care advice for the specific material and finish comes with the piece.
        Drawings and specifications stay on file, so a matching piece later starts from the record
        rather than from scratch.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:var(--space-16)">
      <SectionHead meta="Where we work" level={4}>Service area</SectionHead>
      <p style="max-width:var(--measure)">
        <Value q="q03" />, including {BUSINESS.areaServed.slice(0, -1).join(", ")} and{" "}
        {BUSINESS.areaServed.slice(-1)}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Wrap>

  <EnquireBand heading="If you have a room in mind, start here." chamfer>
    {BAND.body}
    <Fragment slot="facts">
      {BAND.facts.map((q) => (
        <MonoLabel size="md" tone="paper-soft" style="letter-spacing:.1em">
          <Value q={q} />
        </MonoLabel>
      ))}
    </Fragment>
  </EnquireBand>
</Base>
